AltoStaking::deprecateContainer()
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is owner
    ├── given container is already deprecated
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── given container does not exist
    │   └── it should revert
    └── given valid container exists and is not deprecated
        ├── when container is active
        │   ├── it should deprecate container
        │   ├── it should emit ContainerDeprecate event
        │   ├── it should preserve active status
        │   └── when container is max multiplier container
        │       └── it should update max multiplier to next highest active container
        ├── when container is inactive
        │   ├── it should deprecate container
        │   ├── it should emit ContainerDeprecate event
        │   └── it should preserve inactive status
        ├── when container is not max multiplier container
        │   └── it should not change max multiplier container id
        └── when multiple containers are deprecated
            └── it should deprecate all containers while preserving their active status
